MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 107671410882219363}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: de2b5d5ea06784d29910927b98e863a1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PlacedProp
  spec: store_props
  yaw: 270
  rot0: {x: -0.00000001545431, y: 0.7071068, z: -0.00000001545431, w: -0.7071068}
  src: '{"name":"linen_door","floor":"upper","prefab":"Assets/Free Wood Door Pack/Prefab/Wood/Door_3/Door_3_White.prefab","x":[7.168,7.228],"z":[8.846,9.702],"y0":0.0,"height":2.087,"back":"+x","hides":["PropDoor"],"source":"user, Oct 16: ''use one of those white doors from the door pack for the upstairs linen closet''; Door_3 White chosen by the user (four panels, two tall over two tall) over an exact six-panel: the film''s door (art/home_alone/references/foyer-film/upstairs-film-quality-target.png) is a white six-panel colonial, a logged deviation. Leaf = the 30 x 80 in opening (spec/geometry.json linen_closet fake_door, z 8.893-9.655, height 2.032); the pack''s frame adds its own proportions (outer width = leaf x 1.124, height x 1.027, from Wood_Door.FBX: leaf 64.85 x 136.2 cm, frame 72.9 x 139.9 cm), so its panels stretch 1.28x in height. On the hall-side face (x 7.233), 0.5 cm proud, 6 cm deep; the hall-side PropDoor board is hidden, its collider keeps the closet shut."}'
  c0: {x: 7.198, y: 1.0435, z: -9.274}
