  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PlacedProp
  spec: store_props
  yaw: 90
  rot0: {x: 0.00000001545431, y: 0.7071068, z: -0.00000001545431, w: 0.7071068}
  src: '{"name":"rear_passage_end_door","prefab":"Assets/Free Wood Door Pack/Prefab/Wood/Door_3/Door_3_White.prefab","x":[1.585,1.645],"z":[8.91,9.944],"y0":0.0,"height":2.087,"back":"-x","hides":["PropDoor"],"collide":false,"surface":true,"source":"user walk note Oct 18 03:14 (foyer rear, shot 20261018-031353): ''these doors should all be replaced with real doors, the same doors used elsewhere inside'' (overnight 12, not walked). Door_3 White as the other interior doors (linen, girls_a/b, attic, Buzz, parents; the film''s are white six-panel: DEVIATIONS 63h). The pack frame (outer = leaf x 1.124 wide, x 1.027 tall) centred on the opening, 0.5 cm proud of the face, 6 cm deep. Replaces the plain PropDoor slab of the fake door at the rear passage''s end (spec/geometry.json rear_passage|back_hall, x 1.51, z 8.967-9.887: 0.92 m, a 36 in leaf kept at the opening''s width). Film 1690 shows a white panelled door with a brass knob through the arch. Closed: nothing is cut behind it (back_hall is a closed unknown space, DEVIATIONS 22). Hung on the passage face (x 1.58); surface: openings.py stops the baseboard at its frame. The hidden slab''s collider keeps it shut. mirror: the pack''s lever moved to the low-z edge (right as seen from the foyer), as the brass knob in film 1690.","mirror":true}'
  c0: {x: 1.615, y: -1.9825001, z: -9.427}
