  yaw: 180
  rot0: {x: -0, y: 1, z: -0, w: -0.00000004371139}
  src: '{"name":"den_tv","prefab":"Assets/VTC_AV-2062s/Prefabs/VTC_AV-2062s.prefab","x":[2.386,3.072],"z":[17.76,18.48],"y0":0.883,"height":0.6412,"yaw":180,"back":"-x","hides":[],"collide":true,"source":"user-bought CRT TV JVC AV-2049S (Valentyn Bahinskyi, Asset Store; pack VTC_AV-2062s, gitignored). Film 2877/2868: the den''s TV is a black JVC filling the centre bay; measured 0.72 m wide (TV/bay height 0.91 against our 0.777 clear bay). The model is a 20 in set (0.466 x 0.415 x 0.444 m), scaled UNIFORMLY x1.545 into this box (0.72 x 0.641 x 0.686): its tube runs to the bay''s back panel (x 2.385) and its face stands 0.30 m proud of the shelf front (the bookcase''s 0.40 depth is assumed, DEVIATIONS 53/55). On the VCR (top 0.882). yaw 180: the prefab''s screen faces -x at yaw 0 (probed in scratch: 253 vertices across the full 0.466 width at -x vs 12 at +x)"}'
  c0: {x: 2.729, y: -1.8224001, z: -18.119999}
